    REFACTOR-0008: WalkInPrice picks up the concession step

    REFACTOR-0007 gave search() a shared PriceCalculator but left the one
    varying step — concession rates only apply to walk-ins at the counter,
    never to an anonymous search quote — for priceFor to keep handling on
    its own.

    Adds WalkInPrice, the other subclass PriceCalculator was written for:
    it overrides applyConcession() with the real senior/youth discount.
    priceFor now constructs one instead of carrying its own copy of every
    rate. Between this and REFACTOR-0007, neither invoice.ts nor
    parkboard.ts reasons about a rate directly anymore — each just picks
    which price it's computing.

